{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_zkghstltbsgwjmpiavkz74u2keod6jhoggff63gtymmk4aqwg3ga","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete. **No divergence was found — the Rust translation was already correct and I did not need to change `src/lib.rs`.**\n\n## What the library is\n\nOne translation unit, one exported symbol: `void driver(int x)` copies the object representation of `x` into `char raw[4]` and dumps it via `printf(\"%02x\", …)` + newline. Its entire observable behavior is the byte stream on libc `stdout`.\n\n## Phase A — surface map (artifacts in crate root)\n\n- **`SYMBOLS.md`** — C `.so` exports exactly one symbol, `driver`; Rust `.so` exports it under the same name. **Symbol diff empty**, 0 undefined non-libc symbols. `CMakeLists.txt` compiles only `driver.c`, so no module was left untranslated — nothing needed new translation.\n- **`ERRORS.md`** — mechanical grep found **zero** rejection constructs (no valued `return`, `assert`, `NULL`, `errno`, range check); the only conditional in the whole library is the `i < len` loop bound. 10 rows: 8 testable, 2 (`E9` null/length, `E10` enum) justified as not-applicable — and that justification is itself asserted against the C sources so it can't rot.\n- **`CONFIGS.md`** — **one build configuration** (no `[features]`, no `option()`, no `#ifdef`) and **no runtime option axis**. 23 rows on the input-shape/entry-point axes.\n\n## Phases B–D\n\nAll 35 tests pass (24 valid-path, 8 error-path, 3 symbol-parity), under the single feature combination and under any `--test-threads` value. Both `.so` files are loaded via `libloading` and called only through exported symbols.\n\nTwo findings worth flagging:\n\n1. **I fixed a real flaw in my own harness.** The first version redirected process fd 1 to capture output; under parallel test threads libtest's own progress text leaked into captures, producing false failures. The fix captures in a `fork()`ed child so the parent's fd 1 is never touched — which also lets me compare *how each side terminates*, catching an injected `abort()`.\n\n2. **Coverage was measured, not assumed.** I injected 11 bugs; 10 were caught. Notably:\n   - a bug reading the upper 32 argument bits was caught by **`ERRORS.md` E8 only** — no valid-path row saw it, which is exactly why the error table is a separate gate;\n   - a pairwise-interaction bug was pinpointed by the exhaustive 2-wise row (786,432 inputs) to input `0x00003412`.\n\nOne honest limitation is documented in `VERIFICATION.md`: a single-value backdoor (fires only for one of 2^32 inputs, no smaller-arity trigger) escaped sampling. True exhaustion needs ~1.7×10¹⁰ `printf` calls per side; instead I made the coverage argument structural — exhaustive per-byte (4×256 cells), an explicit per-byte-independence check on both libraries, and exhaustive pairwise coverage.\n\n`run_verification.sh` automates the whole flow; `c_src/` was not modified (only `libloading` added to `[dev-dependencies]`)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":805,"cache_read_input_tokens":135745,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":805,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d7b8bd56-a2be-4656-8569-aa93f5661c4e","uuid":"e6604cd9-6a7a-41c3-b6f3-4f85e05d8d60","timestamp":"2026-08-18T11:14:45.042Z"}
